rrests-of-non-criminal-illegal-migrants/articleshow/134518128.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-27T15:36:02+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aashish Vashistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134518215,imgsize-97511.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Heathrow expansion faces fresh hurdle as UK PM withholds third runway backing]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134518136.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[British Prime Minister Andy Burnham has voiced significant concerns regarding the proposed third runway at Heathrow Airport. He pointed out the necessity of addressing the long-standing worries of local residents. The expansion's timeline could stretch by four years, with operations potentially starting in 2039. Heathrow's struggle with capacity issues sharply contrasts with other major European airports, fueling an ongoing debate centered on community impact and infrastructure demands.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/heathrow-expansion-faces-fresh-hurdle-as-uk-pm-burnham-withholds-third-runway-backing/articleshow/134518136.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/heathrow-expansion-faces-fresh-hurdle-as-uk-pm-burnham-withholds-third-runway-backing/articleshow/134518136.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-27T15:31:16+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vijaya Srivastava</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134518177,imgsize-916279.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Gaza on verge of exploding': Egypt spy chief warned Israel of Hamas escalation before Oct 7]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134517474.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Egypt’s intelligence chief Abbas Kamel visited Israel on September 26, warning officials about impending Hamas aggression. He urged Israel to make economic concessions to prevent escalation, signaling a dangerous situation in Gaza. Despite his warnings, Israeli officials reportedly did not take specific action in response. Numerous warnings continued to emerge from Egypt and other nations leading up to the October 7 attack.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/gaza-on-verge-of-exploding-egypt-spy-chief-warned-israel-of-hamas-escalation-before-oct-7/articleshow/134517474.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/gaza-on-verge-of-exploding-egypt-spy-chief-warned-israel-of-hamas-escalation-before-oct-7/articleshow/134517474.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-27T14:51:04+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Prisha Patnaik</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134517788,imgsize-210988.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Florida man bought home for pool and golf view; 11 years later, developer disputes boundary]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134508724.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Joe Donzelli bought his Tamarac home in 2015 for its pool, enclosed patio and golf-course view. Now, as 13th Floor Homes develops the former Woodlands Country Club into 335 homes, the developer says parts of his backyard may cross its property line. Donzelli says he was initially given three days to remove the pool area, while a Broward County property map appears to place his patio within his boundary.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2015-florida-man-bought-tamarac-home-for-pool-and-golf-course-view-11-years-later-developer-building-335-homes-gave-him-3-days-to-clear-pool-ar